<section class="section reveal" id="advanced-stats">
  <span class="section-label">Advanced Techniques</span>
  <h2>Statistical Edge Cases and Numerical Stability</h2>

  <p>Real data is messy. Understanding edge cases prevents silent bugs and incorrect conclusions.</p>

  <h3>Handling Missing Data</h3>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Handling missing data (NaN)</span>
<span class="va">data_with_nan</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">nan</span>, <span class="nm">4</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>])

<span class="cm"># Regular mean includes NaN → result is NaN</span>
<span class="va">mean_with_nan</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">mean</span>(<span class="va">data_with_nan</span>)  <span class="cm"># nan</span>

<span class="cm"># Use nanmean to skip NaN values</span>
<span class="va">mean_skip_nan</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">nanmean</span>(<span class="va">data_with_nan</span>)  <span class="cm"># 3.0</span>

<span class="cm"># Other nan-aware functions: nanstd, nanmedian, nanmin, nanmax</span></code></pre>

  <h3>Weighted Statistics</h3>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Weighted statistics</span>
<span class="va">values</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>])
<span class="va">weights</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>])

<span class="cm"># Weighted mean: (1*1 + 2*2 + 3*3) / (1+2+3) = 14/6 = 2.33</span>
<span class="va">weighted_mean</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">average</span>(<span class="va">values</span>, <span class="va">weights</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">weights</span>)</code></pre>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>NaN propagates through calculations—use nan-aware functions</li>
      <li>Weighted statistics account for importance or frequency of samples</li>
      <li>Always check for outliers before computing statistics</li>
      <li>Consider robust statistics (median, IQR) for skewed data</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

