<section class="section reveal" id="outlier-detection">
  <span class="section-label">Statistical Techniques</span>
  <h2>Outlier Detection Using Statistics</h2>

  <p>Real datasets contain outliers—values that don't fit the main pattern. Detecting and handling outliers is a critical data cleaning task. Statistical methods enable automated outlier detection.</p>

  <h3>IQR Method (Interquartile Range)</h3>

  <p>The IQR method identifies outliers as values beyond 1.5 × IQR from the quartiles. It is robust to extreme values and works with any distribution shape.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Outlier detection with IQR</span>
<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">array</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>, <span class="nm">4</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>, <span class="nm">100</span>, <span class="nm">200</span>])  <span class="cm"># 100, 200 are outliers</span>

<span class="va">Q1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">percentile</span>(<span class="va">data</span>, <span class="nm">25</span>)
<span class="va">Q3</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">percentile</span>(<span class="va">data</span>, <span class="nm">75</span>)
<span class="va">IQR</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">Q3</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="va">Q1</span>

<span class="va">lower_bound</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">Q1</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="nm">1.5</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="va">IQR</span>
<span class="va">upper_bound</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">Q3</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="nm">1.5</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="va">IQR</span>

<span class="va">outliers_mask</span> <span class="op">=</span> (<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op"><</span> <span class="va">lower_bound</span>) <span class="op">|</span> (<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">></span> <span class="va">upper_bound</span>)
<span class="va">outliers</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">data</span>[<span class="va">outliers_mask</span>]

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Outliers detected: {outliers}"</span>)  <span class="cm"># [100 200]</span>

<span class="cm"># Clean data by removing outliers</span>
<span class="va">clean_data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">data</span>[<span class="op">~</span><span class="va">outliers_mask</span>]</code></pre>

  <h3>Z-Score Method</h3>

  <p>Z-score identifies outliers as values beyond 3 standard deviations from the mean. Works best for normally distributed data.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Outlier detection with Z-score</span>
<span class="va">z_scores</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">abs</span>((<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">mean</span>(<span class="va">data</span>)) <span class="op">/</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">std</span>(<span class="va">data</span>))
<span class="va">outliers_z</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">data</span>[<span class="va">z_scores</span> <span class="op">></span> <span class="nm">3</span>]  <span class="cm"># More than 3 std from mean</span></code></pre>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>IQR method is robust to extreme values; use for real data</li>
      <li>Z-score assumes normal distribution; use only when appropriate</li>
      <li>Always visualize outliers before removing—they might be valuable</li>
      <li>Document your outlier handling strategy for reproducibility</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

