<section class="section reveal" id="random-seed-reproducibility">
  <span class="section-label">Advanced</span>
  <h2>Random Seeds and Reproducibility in Production</h2>

  <p>Random number generation is essential for machine learning, but randomness can cause problems in production. Controlling randomness with seeds is crucial for reproducibility and debugging.</p>

  <h3>Seeding Strategy</h3>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Reproducible random number generation</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">numpy</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="im">np</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="im">random</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">set_seed</span>(<span class="va">seed</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">42</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Set seed for all random sources"""</span>
    <span class="cm"># NumPy seed</span>
    <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">random</span>.<span class="fn">seed</span>(<span class="va">seed</span>)

    <span class="cm"># Python's random module</span>
    <span class="fn">random</span>.<span class="fn">seed</span>(<span class="va">seed</span>)

<span class="cm"># Call at start of script</span>
<span class="fn">set_seed</span>(<span class="nm">42</span>)

<span class="cm"># Now all random operations are reproducible</span>
<span class="va">arr1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">random</span>.<span class="fn">randn</span>(<span class="nm">5</span>)
<span class="fn">set_seed</span>(<span class="nm">42</span>)
<span class="va">arr2</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">np</span>.<span class="fn">random</span>.<span class="fn">randn</span>(<span class="nm">5</span>)

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Arrays identical: {np.array_equal(arr1, arr2)}"</span>)  <span class="cm"># True</span></code></pre>

  <h3>When to Seed and When Not To</h3>

  <p><strong>Always seed:</strong> Unit tests, experiments, model training (for reproducibility), bug investigation, demos.</p>
  <p><strong>Never seed:</strong> Monte Carlo simulations (each run should differ), production systems after tuning (use fixed hyperparameters).</p>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Always set seed in research and testing for reproducibility</li>
      <li>Set seed for all random sources (NumPy, Python, TensorFlow)</li>
      <li>Document your seed choice for future reference</li>
      <li>Use np.random.default_rng for new code; RandomState is legacy</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

